{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"5b4ee72a7ddfa8f9b05489da825c368fca943b45057bd6a4e8f86c47e2a181b5","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate","key_entities":["file_impact_scope","no_file_impact_reason","dependency_hashes","compute_validity","_inherited_child_impact","p9_file_impact_coverage","material_fingerprint","FILE_IMPACT event","manifest.py","attest.py","det_lint.py"],"problem_keywords":["file impact","tri-state declaration","undeclared","attestation validity","whole-head invalidation","container poison","explicit none state"],"propositions":["Empty file_impact is overloaded: it conflates undeclared edits with genuinely no-file-impact work, causing conservative whole-HEAD invalidation even for tickets that truthfully touch no repo files.","A tri-state file_impact_scope (undeclared, paths, none) with a required no_file_impact_reason for the none state allows explicit claims to be distinguished from silence.","An explicitly declared none-scope attestation remains valid across unrelated commits and does not poison a parent container's inherited drift scope, while undeclared tickets still trigger whole-HEAD fallback invalidation.","The tri-state declaration is part of the material fingerprint, so transitions between states invalidate the attestation and force re-review."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787897843564657001,"uuid":"ce328759-fe07-4a51-a766-276dcdcf993f"}